+I've completed the read of the full document set (index + sampled module sections deep and shallow, SYSTEM-MODEL, UNIT-MAP, rendered views PDF, panel record, Rumsfeld register, facts ledger, previous quorum verdicts, and spot-verification against source trees). Reference class used: the Apollo Operations Handbook pattern (Section 2 per-subsystem description-of-operation with both sides of every interface, Section 3 malfunction procedures with symptom/cause/remedy), the Spacecraft Familiarization arrangement-first structure, and Flight Data File / mission-rule discipline for limits and switch registers. Note one inventory fact up front: the brief describes "40 module sections, ~22 substantive, ~18 skeleton, 27 components"; the set on disk today is 44 sections (37 stamped VERIFIED, 7 not), 16 components, 18 contracts — the set moved past the brief the same day, and several of its own census numbers moved with it (finding 6 below). I graded what is on disk.
+
+VERDICT: FAIL
+
+STRUCTURE: FAIL — the bound set (docs/master/00-INDEX.md) opens with a per-file census table sorted by path, not a vehicle general arrangement; the general arrangement exists (SYSTEM-MODEL.yaml → cf-system-views.pdf sheets 1-4: master view, component register, contract register) but is orphaned — zero files in docs/master reference SYSTEM-MODEL.yaml, UNIT-MAP.yaml, RUMSFELD.md or the views PDF (grep across docs/ + specs/ finds only the artifacts referencing themselves), and no artifact references module ids back, so no reading path descends from system to section.
+
+SECTIONS STILL FILE-SHAPED: 38 of 44 — every section is titled and scoped by one path (e.g. 01-add_family_lanes, 03-board_lock, 09-clone_lane, 11-disk_floor, 21-lane_target, 22-lib.sh, 35-repo_freshness, the 12/13/14 github-app trio, the 15-18 installers, 26-32 node_* singles); genuinely subsystem-shaped: 6 (04 crier-connect, 05 provisioner, 25 bus worker — both sides named with peer file:function, 33 node ladder, 36 verify ladder, 44 pipeline); subsystem framing exists only in the unbound UNIT-MAP.yaml (M0-M8, 9 modules/25 submodules), which contradicts the section census it is not linked to.
+
+FLOWS MISSING (by class): monitoring (no flow at all — modules 05/25/33 each record "Metrics: NONE" with no compensating procedure); recovery/disaster recovery (admitted absent, 00-INDEX.md:84-85: node loss, key rotation, board or git corruption); degradation/malfunction (8 of 18 contracts are broken/missing per the register but no degraded-mode operating flow exists — the AOH malfunction-procedure class is entirely missing); maintenance (reclaim_disk/freshness/seed-drift units exist, no flow chains them); onboarding a new project (admitted absent); and the five that exist (F1-F5, SYSTEM-MODEL.yaml:249-294, PDF sheets 5-9) are happy-path component sketches: steps name components, never the executing module/unit, carry no per-step measured state, and draw dead steps unannotated — F1 step 6 "completion event" is contract 6 MISSING, F5 steps 2-3 "verdict"/"row closed" sit on contract 13 BROKEN.
+
+CONTRACT GAPS: 18 system contracts exist, all naming both components, 18/18 with payload, 18/18 with measured state (10 works / 6 broken / 2 missing) — but 0 of 18 carry file:function locators on both sides (the master-doc schema's own rule: "a contract with one side named is a rumour", MASTER-DOC-SCHEMA.md:57), 16 of 18 state no timing (only contracts 3 and 8 carry "30 s"), 10 of 18 state no failure semantics; one-sided: 6 systems are documented only from the client side with no page of their own (00-INDEX.md:79-82: scheduler, crier, DuckBrain, 9router, Hermes gateway, bunker daemon) — the serving half of every load-bearing wire; unstated examples: contract 6 (crier→scheduler completion, MISSING, CF-337), contract 9 (node→DuckBrain R1/R2, MISSING, CF-329 — zero DuckBrain calls in the worker).
+
+SETTINGS DOCUMENTED vs EXISTING: 123 of 128 own-surface CLI switches in the 36 module-covered scripts (96%; python argparse 44/47, shell case-arms 79/81) — method: grep add_argument()/case-arm `--x)` in each module's declared Path file vs backticked flags in the module's §7; misses are real (21 `--home`, 44 `--html`/`--out`, 16 `--harness-opts`, 33 `--port`) — but 11 scripts have no module at all (index names only 5; harness_resolve.py, sheet_style.py, verify-patch.sh, gen_nasa/system_views/unit_map carry 22 switches, 0 documented) and the six peer systems' settings are 0 documented anywhere: scheduler lane cadence/weight/pin/admission/cooldown/load-gate, crier env posture (CR_SERVICE_DELIVERY_ALLOWLIST appears only incidentally inside module 25), gateway config, 9router routing, bunker daemon, DuckBrain scoping. Apollo documents every dial; six panels here are dark.
+
+CONTRADICTIONS: 8 —
+1. docs/OPERATIONS.md:209 "it is staged by provisioning" (node-bus-worker.py) vs scripts/node-create.sh:22-23 staged set = {project-node.sh, install-go.sh, lib.sh, disk_floor.py, reclaim_disk.py, harness/harness-vars.sh, harness/install-$HARNESS.sh} — the worker is not staged; module 25 §1 documents the contradiction but OPERATIONS.md, outside the master set, still asserts the false claim where operators read.
+2. docs/RUMSFELD.md:78 (Q1 known-known): "scripts/harness_resolve.py does not exist — measured (ls fails)" vs scripts/harness_resolve.py on disk, 14,274 bytes, commit 74d36cf "feat(harness): harness_resolve.py … Addresses CF-230" (Nov 5, 17:23) — a published known-known that is false on the tree it describes, with no per-row revision stamp or supersede marker.
+3. 00-INDEX.md:71: "scripts/ 43 files … 36 — five scripts still have none" vs the tree: 11 scripts without modules (the five named plus the six above), and 43−36=7 even on its own arithmetic — the census neither names nor counts its gaps correctly.
+4. 00-INDEX.md:71 (43 files / 13,965 lines) vs docs/RUMSFELD.md:60 (42 files / 13,944 lines) — two same-day "measured" censuses of the same directory disagree; Rumsfeld K4 names the question but both numbers are published as fact.
+5. docs/SYSTEM-MODEL.yaml:177 contract 5 note: "only 3 of 14 lanes match the shipped prompt" vs docs/LOOP-CODEX.md:57 D-11 "one node, 17 lanes" (quorum round 1 independently measured 17 code-factory lanes live) — the BROKEN verdict rides an unreconciled denominator, the exact defect class ("603 TICKS") that killed the r2 handbook.
